# AgentLedger — Cursor Rules

## Stack
- Python 3.10+ only
- Core deps: pydantic>=2.0, typer>=0.12, rich>=13.7, mcp>=1.2.0 (MCPServer on mcp 2.x; FastMCP fallback on 1.x)
- Dev deps: pytest>=8.0, ruff>=0.4
- Storage: stdlib sqlite3 only (default `.agentledger/ledger.db` or `:memory:`)

## Code Style
- Strict type hints on all public functions and methods
- Pydantic v2 exclusively: `model_dump()`, `model_dump_json()`, `model_validate()`
- Never use deprecated Pydantic v1 APIs: `.dict()`, `.json()`, `parse_obj()`
- Keep modules under `src/agentledger/` modular and focused

## Engineering
- Provenance Firewall must reject unsigned/invalid EvidenceAnchor receipts before write
- Cascading rollbacks use BFS over causal fact dependencies
- Confidence decay is applied at read time unless explicitly persisted
- After substantive changes, run `pytest` and do not finish until it passes with 0 errors

## CLI / UX
- Prefer Rich `Panel`, `Table`, and `Tree` for high-contrast, minimalist terminal output
